 The given expression is \(8735 + 8736 + 8737 + 8738\). To find the remainder when this sum is divided by 11, we can first find the remainders of each term when divided by 11 and then sum these remainders. The remainders follow a repeating pattern every 11 numbers. Let's find the remainders of 8735, 8736, 8737, and 8738 when divided by 11: \[
8735 \div 11 = 794 \text{ remainder } 1 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 8735 \equiv 1 \pmod{11}
\] \[
8736 \div 11 = 794 \text{ remainder } 2 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 8736 \equiv 2 \pmod{11}
\] \[
8737 \div 11 = 794 \text{ remainder } 3 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 8737 \equiv 3 \pmod{11}
\] \[
8738 \div 11 = 794 \text{ remainder } 4 \quad \Rightarrow \quad 8738 \equiv 4 \pmod{11}
\] The sum of these remainders is \(1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10\). Since \(10 < 11\), the remainder when \(8735 + 8736 + 8737 + 8738\) is divided by 11 is 10. <think> 10 </think> <answer> 10 </answer>

